# Git push
When the user says "push update" (or similar): stage and commit all relevant changes. The agent cannot run `git push` (no GitHub credentials in this environment). After committing, reply in one line that they should run `git push` locally—do not repeat long explanations.

# Links and navigation (CRITICAL — recurring issue, has caused many hours of rework)
- **EVERY nav/dropdown link:** Use plain `<a href="...">`, never Next.js `<Link>` and never `onSelect={() => router.push(...)}`. Radix dropdown + Link blocks navigation; this fails every time we add a new menu item if we forget. Pattern: `<DropdownMenuItem asChild><a href={item.href}>...</a></DropdownMenuItem>`.
- **Before adding or changing any nav/dropdown item:** (1) Use `<a href="...">` for the clickable element. (2) Confirm the route exists (file for that path). (3) Copy the pattern from an existing working dropdown in navbar (e.g. States or Blue).
- **New pages:** Create the route first, then add the link using the same pattern as working items.
